38;2;140;248;247m[48;2;20;22;27m/// After making room fails (every link left is on the screen), how many[35;5H/// more links are refused before trying again: the links and the history's[36;5H/// rows are walked at most once in this many links.[37;5H(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27mconst(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m STALL: (B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27mu32(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m (B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m=(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m (B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m256(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m;   [38;13H[6X[39;7H(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;79;82;88mnk.rs[2;5H[?2026l[?2026h[40;110H(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27mgt[2;5H[?2026l[?2026h[40;110H  [1;11H(B[m[38;2;196;198;205m[48;2;44;46;51m s/link.rs (B[0;1m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m README.md [2;5H(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m# fux-vt-compare: fux-vt beside other terminal emulators[19X[3;5H[77X
An excluded package with its own lockfile. It runs fux-vt beside a panel of[5;5Hother terminal emulators ("engines"):[6;5H[77X
- engines linked into the binary: Ghostty's core (libghostty-vt), alacritty_terminal,[8;5H  libvterm, avt, wezterm-term and the vt100 crate;[25X[9;5H- engines run as processes of their own: xterm.js (`@xterm/headless` under  [10;5H  Node), tmux, and xterm itself under Xvfb.[33X[11;5H[22X
Every engine gets the same output. After each piece of it, and each resize,[13;5Heach engine's screen is compared with fux-vt's, cell by cell, along with the [14;5Hcursor, the modes, soft wraps, the title, cursor reports and recent history.[15;5Hfux-vt fails a case only where the engines outvote it (see "The vote"). A[16;5Hfailing case is shrunk to the smallest one that still fails and printed with[17;5Hthe command that replays it. `bench` times every engine on the same[18;5Hworkloads. The corpus (`corpus/`) holds what real programs wrote to a[19;5Hterminal, recorded by `record`.[20;5H[72X
It is not built or run by fux's own gates. It needs Zig, a Ghostty[22;5Hcheckout, libvterm's source and, for the engines in their own processes,[23;5HNode, tmux, xterm and Xvfb. `run.sh` fetches the first three.[14X[24;5H[41X
No engine is the truth. When the panel outvotes fux-vt, the difference says[26;5Hwhere to look. xterm's behaviour and the standards decide which side is[7X[27;5Hright. Some differences are choices fux-vt makes on purpose, and each family[28;5Hbelow records which.[54X[29;5H[45X
